SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday? Hike-  Robert Kinsley Nature Preserve & part of Maso
 n Dixon Trail
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nHike coordinator: Jan Zer
 foss 717-201-0530\n\n\\~4.5 miles. Yellow\, orange\, blue (Mason Dixon Tra
 il) along Wild Cat run and falls and on to Wildcat Bluff overlook\, yellow
  to Buzzards Roost overlook\, blue\, red\, yellow. Actual distance and rou
 te subject to change based on day-of weather and trail conditions. Or\, we
  may do this route in reverse.\n\n[Robert Kinsley Nature Preserve website 
 and trail map](https://www.lancasterconservancy.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 5/06/Robert-A-Kinsley-Trail-Map_20250611.pdf)\n[Alltrails ](https://www.al
 ltrails.com/explore/trail/us/pennsylvania/mason-dixon-trail-hellam-hills)W
 e'll hike parts of this and in a different order.\n\nThere are NO toilet f
 acilities at this area.\n\nPlease bring your own water and energy snack an
 d first aid kit. I always strongly encourage bringing hiking poles. **Plea
 se be sure to familiarize yourself with the route and terrain to make sure
  this hike is within your capabilities.**\n\nIt is hunting season so pleas
 e remember to wear blaze orange or some other high viz clothing.\n\nAfter 
 hike coffee/lunch: TBD\, open to suggestions.\n\nTo eliminate passing arou
 nd a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP
  below to join this ride. Being on\nMeetup does not mean you are a club me
 mber. Join here [Member Signup](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.
 aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\n\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by
  the club's Code of Conduct: [Code of Conduct](https://www.lancasterbikecl
 ub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\n\nGuidanc
 e if an incident occurs: [Incident Actions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/
 content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=326137)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3174111
 99/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
